# HealthCoach .cursorrules
# These rules govern every Composer session in this project.
# Do not override or remove them.

## Project identity
- iOS 26+ target, SwiftUI, SwiftData, ObjectBox (via SPM). No other persistence frameworks.
- Deployment device: iPhone 16 Pro (A18 Pro, Apple Intelligence enabled).
- Privacy-first: no health data leaves the device at runtime. No cloud SDKs, remote logging, analytics, or telemetry packages.

## Scope discipline
- Build ONLY the milestone explicitly stated in the current task prompt.
- Do not implement milestones that have not been requested yet.
- Do not refactor, rename, or restructure files from previous milestones unless the current milestone explicitly names them.
- Do not add features, abstractions, error handling, or comments not required by the current milestone's accept criteria.
- If the milestone does not mention a file, do not touch it.

## Loop and cost guardrails
- If a build or test fails after 2 attempts, STOP. Output the full error verbatim and wait for instruction.
- Do not run the same terminal command more than twice. If it fails twice, report and stop.
- If an SPM package, framework, or API is unavailable or does not compile, STOP and report. Do not search for or propose alternative packages.
- Do not install SPM packages not listed in the approved plan.
- Do not make any network requests at runtime.

## Swift and iOS conventions
- Use os.Logger for all logging. Every data-path function must log entry, key counts, and exit.
  Logger categories: healthkit, import, vectorstore, embedding, sync, ui, recovery.
- Never load the Apple Health export.xml into memory whole. Use streaming XMLParser.
- Always call the HealthKit observer query completionHandler immediately after setting the dirty flag.
  Skipping it permanently disables background delivery.
- Never fire concurrent requests to a LanguageModelSession (V2+).
  Bind all submit UI to session.isResponding.
- Use Color.black for OLED dark mode backgrounds, not system dark gray.
- No em dashes, en dashes, or double dashes in any code, comments, strings, or UI copy. Rewrite the sentence.

## Code style
- No comments explaining what code does. Only add a comment when the why is non-obvious.
- No trailing summaries or change-log comments at the top of files.
- No unused imports.
- Prefer editing existing files to creating new ones.

## Commit gate
- After completing a milestone and confirming the accept criteria pass, output exactly:
  MILESTONE COMPLETE: <milestone name>
  READY TO COMMIT
  Do not proceed to the next milestone until instructed.
